// GAP-ZYB-001 — the decimal count can be computed, not only written.
//
// `#,.N|…|` and its family took a literal, so a formatter whose precision
// arrives at run time could not use them at all. For money the count IS
// configuration: the Chilean peso has no minor unit in circulation (exponent
// 0), the euro and the dollar have two, the Kuwaiti dinar three. The exponent
// belongs to the CURRENCY, not to the program, so ZyBank wrote forty lines of
// integer arithmetic — separate the sign, divide by 10^exponent, pad the
// remainder, group the thousands — and `zyquality/bench/lib_time.zy` had
// patched the same hole in the small, padding milliseconds with a three-branch
// chain. Two unrelated programs writing the same workaround is the sign that
// something is missing from the language and not from the programs.
//
// A written count keeps its fast path: the VM still encodes it as an immediate
// operand, and only a computed one costs a register.
n = 2
e = 3

>> "escrito:    " #,.2|10.5| ¶
>> "calculado:  " #,.n|10.5| ¶
>> "otro:       " #,.e|1234.5678| ¶

// The whole family takes it.
>> "redondear:  " #.n|10.567| ¶
>> "truncar:    " #!n|10.567| ¶
>> "científico: " #^.n|12345.678| ¶

// A name and not a general expression, deliberately: the `|` that opens the
// value is also how bitwise-or is spelled, and the browser engine lexes this
// count inside the token. Compute it into a name first if it is more than one.
ancho = n + 1
>> "calculado2: " #,.ancho|10.5| ¶

// And it reads a parameter, which is the case that matters: the count comes
// from the currency the function was handed.
formatear(importe, exp) { <~ #,.exp|importe| }
>> "peso:       " formatear(25990, 0) ¶
>> "euro:       " formatear(25.99, 2) ¶
>> "dinar:      " formatear(25.99, 3) ¶

// Zero decimals is a count like any other, and not "no count".
>> "cero:       " #,.0|1234.9| ¶
c = 0
>> "cero calc.: " #,.c|1234.9| ¶
